      "worked": "The denominators are $(x-1)^2+2>0$ and $(x+1)^2+2>0$, so the domain is $\\mathbb{R}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{(-x-1)^2}{(-x)^2-2(-x)+3}+\\frac{(-x+1)^2}{(-x)^2+2(-x)+3}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{(x+1)^2}{x^2+2x+3}+\\frac{(x-1)^2}{x^2-2x+3}\\\\f(-x)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $f$ is even.",
